{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":1694136,"num_turns":36,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7f72f211-6999-477a-b56b-b4dc8b777f58","total_cost_usd":4.828009999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":375985,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":94848,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":375987,"outputTokens":97914,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":80036,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":4.828009999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Done. **16/16 workloads pass with `max_abs = 0.000e+00` — bit-identical to the reference**, not merely within tolerance.\n\n## What the problem actually was\n\nThe obvious optimization is a trap. Since the projection is row-wise, `cat([E,H]) @ Wᵀ` then split is algebraically identical to projecting each stream separately — skipping the concat entirely. I tested it rather than assuming, and it **fails 4 of 16 workloads**, with matched ratios as low as **0.082** against a required 0.99.\n\nThe cause: tolerance here is ~1 ULP of fp32, and hipBLASLt picks its algorithm from the problem shape. At small M it switches to a split-K reduction with a different accumulation order. The reference's *order of operations is part of the spec*, so the fused GEMM had to be preserved exactly. Had I shipped that \"obvious\" win, it would have passed a casual eyeball check and scored zero.\n\n## Where the headroom actually was\n\nI profiled instead of guessing, which redirected the work:\n\n- **GEMM: 97% of runtime, but already at 94.1 / 95.5 TFLOP/s — 98.5% of the fp32 ceiling.** I confirmed this two ways: a Triton GEMM reached only 79 TFLOP/s *and* broke bit-exactness (`tl.dot` silently uses tf32), and standalone square GEMMs cap at 95.5. There is essentially nothing to win here.\n- **tf32 would be 4x faster** (380 TFLOP/s) — and is disqualifying at this tolerance. Noted and rejected.\n- **Concat: only 3%, but running at 4.2 TB/s** — genuinely slow, and pure data movement, so *any* correct copy is bit-exact by construction. Zero numerical risk.\n\nSo the concat was the only safe target. The winning design makes `BLOCK` divide `hidden_dim=3072`, so each program stays within one row and the row index plus source-tensor selection become **scalar** per program — no vector integer division by a non-power-of-two, no per-element masking, fully coalesced. That hit **6.77 TB/s, matching `torch.clone`'s measured ceiling.** Two rejected alternatives: a 2D-grid variant crashed Triton's AMD buffer-ops pass, and a two-kernel version doubled launch overhead.\n\nBelow ~24 MB the ~12 µs launch cost exceeds the bandwidth gain, so `torch.cat` is used. That threshold is a measured crossover between two fully general implementations — both paths compute identical results for any input; it is not a shape special-case.\n\n## Honest assessment of the result\n\nEnd-to-end speedup is **1.01x**, and that is the ceiling, not a shortfall. This problem is one large fp32 GEMM that hipBLASLt already runs at 98.5% of hardware peak. I removed ~33% of the concat's time, but Amdahl's law caps the total at ~1%. Since scoring is proximity to the Speed-of-Light bound rather than speedup over the reference, being pinned to the fp32 roofline is the right outcome — the only way to go meaningfully faster would be reduced precision, which the tolerance forbids.\n\nI also verified robustness beyond the given workloads (`t=1`, `i=1`, non-contiguous inputs and weights, threshold boundaries, 28k-row index ranges, call-to-call determinism) — all bit-exact. Two of five attempts used; scratch files removed, leaving `kernel.py` and `solution.json`.","ttft_ms":5262,"ttft_stream_ms":5261,"time_to_request_ms":91,"type":"result","duration_ms":1770959,"uuid":"84ae6206-9147-4062-ad7f-5b76b9313597"}
